# @@PKG@@ — COCO Lab level `@@LEVEL_ID@@`, scenario `@@SCENARIO@@`, in ROS 2

@@TITLE@@. Generated by COCO Lab (`coco_lab.level_package`) from the level's World Spec: the Gazebo
world, the Nav2 map and parameters, and @@N_GOALS@@ goal(s) from the start (@@START_X@@, @@START_Y@@,
θ @@START_THETA@@). What runs is COCO's real ROS 2 stack (Jazzy, Gazebo Harmonic, Nav2, cmd_vel_arbiter):
a **simulation**, labelled STACK; no physical robot exists.

## What it needs

ROS 2 Jazzy and COCO's robot packages from COCO Lab's repository (`gazebo_models`: the robot and its
Gazebo + Nav2 bring-up; `custom_teleop`: `cmd_vel_arbiter`). Stock Jazzy alone does not have COCO.
Two verified ways:

### A. In COCO's image (nothing else to install)

```bash
# in the folder that holds @@PKG@@/
docker run --rm -it --ulimit core=0 -v "$PWD/@@PKG@@:/ws/src/@@PKG@@" --entrypoint bash \
  ghcr.io/gauthamcodes/coco-ros2 -c '
  source /opt/ros/jazzy/setup.bash && source /opt/coco_ws/install/setup.bash &&
  cd /ws && colcon build --packages-select @@PKG@@ && source install/setup.bash &&
  (ros2 launch @@PKG@@ level.launch.py > launch.log 2>&1 &) &&
  ros2 run @@PKG@@ run_goals --out /ws/src/@@PKG@@/results.json'
```

The results land in `@@PKG@@/results.json` on your machine.

### B. On your own ROS 2 Jazzy install

```bash
git clone https://github.com/GauthamCodes/coco-labs && cd coco-labs
scripts/build_overlay.sh ~/coco_ws            # COCO's packages, built from the repository
export COCO_WS=~/coco_ws && source setup_env.sh
mkdir -p ~/coco_level_ws/src && cp -r /path/to/@@PKG@@ ~/coco_level_ws/src/
cd ~/coco_level_ws && colcon build --symlink-install && source install/setup.bash
ros2 launch @@PKG@@ level.launch.py gui:=true      # terminal 1
ros2 run @@PKG@@ run_goals                          # terminal 2 (after "bring-up done")
```

## Your own algorithm

Export it from COCO Lab's Studio ("Export as ROS 2 package"), put `coco_user_<name>/` beside this
package, build both, and launch with `user_package:=coco_user_<name>`: its node replaces the matching
Nav2 component; the wheels still go through `cmd_vel_arbiter`.

## What is in here

- `level/gazebo/@@LEVEL_ID@@.sdf` — the world (COCO Lab's `worldgen`, from the World Spec);
- `level/nav2/@@LEVEL_ID@@.yaml`, `.pgm` — the map; `level/nav2/nav2_params.yaml` — COCO's Nav2
  parameters for this level (derivation @@DERIVATION@@; every change and why: `params_derivation.json`);
- `level/gazebo/diff_drive_calibration.yaml` — the odometry calibration `bringup` loads;
- `scenario.json` — the goals; `launch/level.launch.py`; `@@PKG@@/bringup.py`, `@@PKG@@/run_goals.py`.

Limits, stated: the Depot's forklifts and walkers stand still here (COCO Lab's recordings drove them with
a scenario script that is not part of this package); `run_goals` reports Nav2's verdict and AMCL's
distance to each goal, not Gazebo's ground truth. Files: sha256 in `level/checksums.json`.
